Rule 1 (tensor shape matches given tuple shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = v_2.len ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = v_2[i]
>>
Rule 2 (tensor has correct dimensionality for outer product)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1
>>
Rule 4 (tensor size matches outer product dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_3, 0)
>>
Rule 5 (input tensor is empty or only contains non-negative values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ min(v_1) ≥ 0
